        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: This shows you how the <color=#0FF>D2dDestructibleSprite</color> component's
        <color=#0FF>SolidRange</color> setting can be used to create pixels that
        are harder or impossible to destroy. When this is set, pixels with an alpha
        of 255 will be impossible to destroy, and pixels within the range will be
        increasingly easier to destroy. The optional <color=#0FF>SolidMask</color>
        setting can be used to easily define which pixels fall within this range.
        Keep in mind that you must click <color=#0FF>Rebuild</color> for the mask
        changes to update.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
